<blurb shelf="Mathematics">
      This trigonometry textbook should be suitable for a one-semester course in trigonometry, useful to students in a variety of programs.  For example, students who have encountered elements of triangle trig in previous courses may be able to skip all or part of Chapters 1 through 3.  Students preparing for technical courses may not need much of the material after Chapter 6 or 7.  Chapters 9 and 10 cover vectors and polar coordinates, optional topics that occur in some trigonometry courses but are often reserved for precalculus.
